{title: Glass Houses}
{artist: Penny Marlowe}

{start_of_verse}
[Dm]We built it out [Bb]of windows
[F]So the neighbours [C]all could see
[Dm]Every dish we br[Bb]oke on Sundays
[F]Every word you said [C]to me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Bb]Glass houses[F], glass houses
[C]Don't you throw [Dm]that stone
[Bb]Glass houses[F], glass houses
[C]We were never qui[Dm]te alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Dm]Now the windows [Bb]have a crack in
[F]Shaped exactly li[C]ke the moon
[Dm]And the light g[Bb]ets in at midnight
[F]Like it's going t[C]o leave you soon
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Bb]Glass houses[F], glass houses
[C]Don't you throw [Dm]that stone
[Bb]Glass houses[F], glass houses
[C]We were never qui[Dm]te alone
{end_of_verse}
